            if good:\n272:                 verified.append(direction)\n273:             else:\n274:                 timed_out = timed_out or is_timeout(log)\n275:                 rec[f\"{direction}_log_tail\"] = log.strip()[-800:]\n276: \n277:         if len(verified) == 2:\n278:             # Both `Candidate` and `¬ Candidate` accepted means the environment\n279:             # proves False. Never report that as a resolution.\n280:             rec.update(status=\"INCONSISTENT\", reason=\"both directions kernel-verified\")\n281:             counts[\"INCONSISTENT\"] += 1\n282:             print(f\"  {ident}  !!! BOTH DIRECTIONS VERIFIED — inconsistency, investigate\")\n283:         elif verified:\n284:             d = verified[0]\n285:             expected = {\"true\": \"prove\", \"false\": \"refute\"}.get(str(rec[\"label\"]).lower())\n286:             if args.strict and expected and d != expected:\n287:                 rec.update(status=\"wrong_direction\", direction=d)\n288:                 counts[\"wrong_direction\"] += 1\n289:                 print(f\"  {ident}  WRONG DIRECTION: {d} but label={rec['label']}\")\n290:             else:\n291:                 rec.update(status=\"resolved\", direction=d)\n292:                 counts[\"resolved\"] += 1\n293:                 print(f\"  {ident}  RESOLVED by {d}\")\n294:         else:\n295:             status = \"timeout\" if timed_out else \"unresolved\"\n296:             rec.update(status=status)\n297:             counts[status] += 1\n298:             print(f\"  {ident}  {status}\")\n299:         results.append(rec)\n300: \n301:     out = os.path.join(args.dir, f\"verification_{args.partition}.json\")\n302:     json.dump(results, open(out, \"w\"), indent=1)\n303:     print(f\"\\npartition '{args.partition}': {len(index)} items, {len(results)} files returned\")\n304:     for k in (\"resolved\", \"unresolved\", \"timeout\", \"rejected\", \"wrong_direction\",\n305:               \"INCONSISTENT\"):\n306:         print(f\"  {k:16s}: {counts[k]}\")\n307:     print(f\"  -> {out}\")\n308:     return 0\n309: \n310: \n311: def do_lint(args) -> int:\n312:     try:\n313:         text = open(args.file).read()\n314:     except Exception as e:\n315:         print(f\"LINT: cannot read {args.file}: {e}\")\n316:         return 2\n317:     original = open(args.original).read() if args.original else None\n318:     ok, why = lint_text(text, original)\n319:     print(\"LINT: ok\" if ok else f\"LINT: REJECTED — {why}\")\n320:     return 0 if ok else 1\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":166,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:50:46Z","thinking":"**Constructing proof structure**\n\nThe code defines a function that appears to generate elements for a formal proof.  It normalizes input and determines the direction (prove or refute). Based on the direction, a corresponding header and pristine (initial) proof structure are generated.  The core structure establishes the theorem statement and its initial 'by' clause for subsequent proof steps.\n\n\n**Analyzing proof verification structure**\n\nThe code generates verification theorems by analyzing the generated proof attempt. It strips parts of the original attempt and confirms its structure. The function ensures the proof's target type matches the expected type, constructing a verification theorem from the original proof's result. This verification theorem essentially asserts that the original theorem is indeed of the claimed type.\n\n\n**Verifying generated file structure**\n\nThe task involves generating a specific Lean file structure. It necessitates preserving code up to a definition, followed by helper lemmas, and then prove/refute theorems. The script checks for the correct structure, verifying the presence of the `Candidate` definition, lemmas and the theorem statements. This validation includes the format and the correctness of the generated `lean` file.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > Challenge_1facfd37.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\n\nopen SimpleGraph\n\n-- Conjecture under test: (nontrivial) ⇒ independence_number ≤ edge_cover_number\n-- Both declarations refer to the same `Candidate`.\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasEdgeCover G → GraphCalc.indepNum G ≤ GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber G\n\nlemma sym2_eq_of_ne_mem {V : Type*} [DecidableEq V] (u v : V) (e : Sym2 V)\n    (hu : u ∈ e) (hv : v ∈ e) (hne : u ≠ v) : e = s(u, v) := by\n  induction e using Sym2.inductionOn with\n  | hf a b =>\n    rw [Sym2.mem_iff] at hu hv\n    rcases hu with rfl | rfl <;> rcases hv with rfl | rfl\n    · contradiction\n    · rfl\n    · exact Sym2.eq_swap\n    · contradiction\n\nlemma indep_card_le_edge_cover_card {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (I : Finset V) (hI : GraphCalc.IsIndependentFinset G I)\n    (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) (hs_sub : s ⊆ G.edgeFinset) (hs_cov : GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s) :\n    I.card ≤ s.card := by\n  let f : V → Sym2 V := fun v => Classical.choose (hs_cov v)\n  have hf_spec : ∀ v, f v ∈ s ∧ v ∈ f v := fun v => Classical.choose_spec (hs_cov v)\n  have hmaps : Set.MapsTo f (↑I) (↑s) := by\n    intro v _\n    exact (hf_spec v).1\n  have hinj : Set.InjOn f (↑I) := by\n    intro u hu v hv heq\n    by_contra hne\n    have hu_e : u ∈ f u := (hf_spec u).2\n    have hv_e : v ∈ f u := by rw [heq]; exact (hf_spec v).2\n    have he_eq : f u = s(u, v) := sym2_eq_of_ne_mem u v (f u) hu_e hv_e hne\n    have he_in_s : f u ∈ s := (hf_spec u).1\n    have he_in_edges : f u ∈ G.edgeFinset := hs_sub he_in_s\n    rw [SimpleGraph.mem_edgeFinset] at he_in_edges\n    rw [he_eq] at he_in_edges\n    rw [SimpleGraph.mem_edgeSet] at he_in_edges\n    have h_not_adj : ¬ G.Adj u v := hI u hu v hv\n    exact h_not_adj he_in_edges\n  exact Finset.card_le_card_of_injOn f hmaps hinj\n\ntheorem prove_1facfd37 : Candidate := by\n  intro V _ _ G _ _ _\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.indepNum, GraphCalc.edgeCoverNumber, GraphCalc.minUpTo]\n  cases hmax : ((Finset.univ.powerset.filter (GraphCalc.IsIndependentFinset G)).image Finset.card).max with\n  | bot =>\n    exact Nat.zero_le _\n  | coe alpha =>\n    change alpha ≤ Option.getD (((Finset.range (Fintype.card V + 1)).filter\n      (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s)).min) (Fintype.card V)\n    have h_alpha_mem : alpha ∈ ((Finset.univ.powerset.filter (GraphCalc.IsIndependentFinset G)).image Finset.card) :=\n      Finset.mem_of_max hmax\n    rw [Finset.mem_image] at h_alpha_mem\n    rcases h_alpha_mem with ⟨I, hI, hI_card⟩\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hI\n    have hI_indep : GraphCalc.IsIndependentFinset G I := hI.2\n    cases hmin : (((Finset.range (Fintype.card V + 1)).filter\n      (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s)).min) with\n    | top =>\n      change alpha ≤ Fintype.card V\n      subst hI_card\n      exact Finset.card_le_univ I\n    | coe rho =>\n      change alpha ≤ rho\n      have h_rho_mem : rho ∈ (((Finset.range (Fintype.card V + 1)).filter\n        (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, GraphCalc.IsEdgeCoverFinset G s))) :=\n        Finset.mem_of_min hmin\n      rw [Finset.mem_filter] at h_rho_mem\n      rcases h_rho_mem.2 with ⟨s, hs_pow, hs_cov⟩\n      rw [Finset.mem_powersetCard] at hs_pow\n      have hs_sub : s ⊆ G.edgeFinset := hs_pow.1\n      have hs_card : s.card = rho := hs_pow.2\n      have h_le := indep_card_le_edge_cover_card G I hI_indep s hs_sub hs_cov\n      rw [hI_card, hs_card] at h_le\n      exact h_le\n\ntheorem refute_1facfd37 : ¬ Candidate := by\n  sorry\n\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_1facfd37.lean\n","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_1facfd37","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Updating Challenge_1facfd37.lean and checking","toolSummary":"Update and check Challenge_1facfd37.lean"}}]}
